    "result_text": "Done. All changes are in and the suite is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## What changed\n\nThe household is now keyed on **(lastName, postcode)** and derived deterministically, so shared households need no stored link.\n\n**`Household.id(lastName, postcode)`** \u2014 now takes postcode instead of address and returns the **first 12 hex chars** of `SHA-256(normalize(lastName) + \"|\" + postcode)` (was 16 hex over `lastName|address`). `normalize` (trim/collapse-whitespace/lowercase) still applies to the last name; postcode is used as given (null-guarded to `\"\"`).\n\n**`RequireUniqueIdentity`** (the duplicate block) \u2014 now also rejects a **household duplicate** (an existing owner with the same computed `householdId`) as **409**, *bypassed when the request sets `sharesHousehold`*. The pre-existing contact-key (telephone+email) collision check is kept \u2014 `sharesHousehold` does not bypass that, since a declared member is still a distinct contact.\n\n**`FlagPossibleDuplicate`** \u2014 a **declared member** (`sharesHousehold=true`) is no longer flagged: `possibleDuplicate=false`, `possibleDuplicateOf=null`. It reads `sharesHousehold` via the published `OwnerFieldsDto` variable. (Any non-declared owner sharing lastName+postcode is now rejected upstream, so this is the only path that shares a household and survives.)\n\n**`CountHouseholdMembers`** \u2014 the household-size count now keys off the computed `householdId` (postcode-based).\n\n**`OwnerIdentity.key` / `OwnerMapper`** \u2014 the `householdId` and `identityKey` response fields now derive from postcode instead of address.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 updated the `sharesHousehold` and `householdId` descriptions to match the new (lastName, postcode) semantics.\n\n## Behaviour now matches the spec\n- Same lastName + postcode \u21d2 same `householdId` automatically (no stored link).\n- A second owner in an existing household \u21d2 **409**, unless `sharesHousehold` \u21d2 created as a declared member.\n- A declared member is **not** flagged as a possible duplicate.\n- Duplicate detection and household sizing both key off the computed `householdId`.\n\nThe `AcceptanceTest` (`coreSameLastNameAndPostcodeShareHouseholdId`) \u2014 which uses `sharesHousehold` to bypass the block and asserts equal `householdId` for same lastName+postcode and differing for a different lastName \u2014 passes.",
